# LAWP

This repo is **LAWP** (Learn Anything While Playing) — a standalone Windows Electron + React LMS.

## Isolation

- Do **not** import, copy from, or depend on any other application repo.
- Specs live in `docs/`. Implement against those files. Update `docs/DECISIONS.md` when behavior is locked.

## Architecture

- Electron main owns packs (zip install/export), runners, learners, progress, settings, window state.
- Renderer is React + Zustand; **no Node integration**.
- Typed preload IPC + Zod; Result `{ ok, value } | { ok: false, error }`.
- App state only under Electron `userData` (`%APPDATA%\LAWP` for both `npm run dev` and installed builds). Installer never writes that folder.

## Must preserve

- Window size, position, maximized state across sessions (`window-state.json`).
- Shared AppData unless `LAWP_USER_DATA` or `LAWP_ISOLATED_USER_DATA=1`. Dist/reinstall must not overwrite settings or `userData/packs`.
- Custom app icon, never the default Electron icon.
- Self-contained `tsconfig.json` / `tsconfig.node.json` / `tsconfig.web.json` (no missing `extends` packages).

## Content

- Generalized **JSON cartridges** (closed vocabulary, AI-generable): one folder per pack, one folder per lesson. `activity` / `world-v1` for any subject; code engines optional. Install/export as `.zip`.
- Progress: bounded activity log + durable evidence + snapshots under `userData/learners/<id>/`. Restart keeps history.
- Why panel + misconceptions; conceptual hints free; imported code packs untrusted until allowed.
- Original lessons only. Do not scrape or reproduce Codefinity materials.
- First demo: circuits 20-minute spike; then Python, JavaScript, React.

## Settings

- Every new preference goes on `settingsSchema` so export/import round-trips it.
- Strip window geometry (and secrets by default) from export. Optional setup bundle = settings + user cartridges; import merges, never silent overwrite.
- Library is a runtime union of app `resources/packs` and `%APPDATA%\LAWP\packs` (user wins). Not a build-time catalog.
